{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_silSBGoJAdpzZRzfNbxO5a3U|fc_0f43adc3108fe495016a95466ac88487d2b825cae65f85500e","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Write interface repair report","path":"/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","content":"# Interface Fix Report\n\n## Root cause\n\n`orders.adapter` still read the removed `product.price_cents` attribute for catalog `Product` objects. It also read `product.currency`, but currency now belongs to the nested `Money` value at `product.price.currency`. As a result, new catalog products failed during pricing and could incorrectly default to USD during currency checks.\n\n## Changed files\n\n- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py` — read `amount_cents` and `currency` from the nested `Money` object for new catalog products, while retaining `price_cents` and the optional `currency` field for legacy product dictionaries.\n\nThe `orders.service` currency comparison remains active, so differing currencies in one order raise `ValueError(\"mixed currencies are not supported\")`. The `catalog` `Money` model was not changed.\n\n## Verification command\n\n- `python -m pytest tests`\n\nThe requested command was attempted in the provided workspace, but its environment has no `python` executable and `/usr/bin/python3` has no `pytest` module. A direct Python smoke check was run with the repository package paths and covered new `Money` products, legacy dictionaries, reports grouped by currency, and mixed-currency rejection.\n"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0f43adc3108fe495016a95466906d087d29391dc69267985ac\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough\":{\"turn_id\":\"a6dc917d-8380-443b-a68d-d6fac1f69967\"},\"summary\":[],\"metadata\":{\"turn_id\":\"a6dc917d-8380-443b-a68d-d6fac1f69967\"}}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_silSBGoJAdpzZRzfNbxO5a3U|fc_0f43adc3108fe495016a95466ac88487d2b825cae65f85500e","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Write interface repair report","path":"/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","content":"# Interface Fix Report\n\n## Root cause\n\n`orders.adapter` still read the removed `product.price_cents` attribute for catalog `Product` objects. It also read `product.currency`, but currency now belongs to the nested `Money` value at `product.price.currency`. As a result, new catalog products failed during pricing and could incorrectly default to USD during currency checks.\n\n## Changed files\n\n- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py` — read `amount_cents` and `currency` from the nested `Money` object for new catalog products, while retaining `price_cents` and the optional `currency` field for legacy product dictionaries.\n\nThe `orders.service` currency comparison remains active, so differing currencies in one order raise `ValueError(\"mixed currencies are not supported\")`. The `catalog` `Money` model was not changed.\n\n## Verification command\n\n- `python -m pytest tests`\n\nThe requested command was attempted in the provided workspace, but its environment has no `python` executable and `/usr/bin/python3` has no `pytest` module. A direct Python smoke check was run with the repository package paths and covered new `Money` products, legacy dictionaries, reports grouped by currency, and mixed-currency rejection.\n"},"intent":"Write interface repair report"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":4377,"output":385,"cacheRead":16128,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20890,"reasoningTokens":88,"cost":{"input":0.0008754,"output":0.00046199999999999995,"cacheRead":0.00032256,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0016599599999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788167784163,"responseId":"resp_0f43adc3108fe495016a95466872bc87d2968eabd056335fe5","duration":7909.3706549999915,"ttft":904.3007139999972}}
{"type":"tool_execution_start","toolCallId":"call_silSBGoJAdpzZRzfNbxO5a3U|fc_0f43adc3108fe495016a95466ac88487d2b825cae65f85500e","toolName":"write","args":{"path":"/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","content":"# Interface Fix Report\n\n## Root cause\n\n`orders.adapter` still read the removed `product.price_cents` attribute for catalog `Product` objects. It also read `product.currency`, but currency now belongs to the nested `Money` value at `product.price.currency`. As a result, new catalog products failed during pricing and could incorrectly default to USD during currency checks.\n\n## Changed files\n\n- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py` — read `amount_cents` and `currency` from the nested `Money` object for new catalog products, while retaining `price_cents` and the optional `currency` field for legacy product dictionaries.\n\nThe `orders.service` currency comparison remains active, so differing currencies in one order raise `ValueError(\"mixed currencies are not supported\")`. The `catalog` `Money` model was not changed.\n\n## Verification command\n\n- `python -m pytest tests`\n\nThe requested command was attempted in the provided workspace, but its environment has no `python` executable and `/usr/bin/python3` has no `pytest` module. A direct Python smoke check was run with the repository package paths and covered new `Money` products, legacy dictionaries, reports grouped by currency, and mixed-currency rejection.\n"},"intent":"Write interface repair report"}
{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_silSBGoJAdpzZRzfNbxO5a3U|fc_0f43adc3108fe495016a95466ac88487d2b825cae65f85500e","toolName":"write","args":{"path":"/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","content":"# Interface Fix Report\n\n## Root cause\n\n`orders.adapter` still read the removed `product.price_cents` attribute for catalog `Product` objects. It also read `product.currency`, but currency now belongs to the nested `Money` value at `product.price.currency`. As a result, new catalog products failed during pricing and could incorrectly default to USD during currency checks.\n\n## Changed files\n\n- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py` — read `amount_cents` and `currency` from the nested `Money` object for new catalog products, while retaining `price_cents` and the optional `currency` field for legacy product dictionaries.\n\nThe `orders.service` currency comparison remains active, so differing currencies in one order raise `ValueError(\"mixed currencies are not supported\")`. The `catalog` `Money` model was not changed.\n\n## Verification command\n\n- `python -m pytest tests`\n\nThe requested command was attempted in the provided workspace, but its environment has no `python` executable and `/usr/bin/python3` has no `pytest` module. A direct Python smoke check was run with the repository package paths and covered new `Money` products, legacy dictionaries, reports grouped by currency, and mixed-currency rejection.\n"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing 1215 bytes to out/interface_fix_report.md..."}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md"}}}
